# QA loop

Run **from `front-end/`** after any Vue/TypeScript/CSS change. Fix failures before continuing.

Frontend mise tasks use the current config-root prefix (`:`). Do not run them from the repo root (`mise check` / `mise //front-end:check` are not the frontend workflow).

```bash
cd front-end          # required — this is the config root
mise :type-check      # vue-tsc --build
mise :format:check    # oxfmt --check src/  (fix with mise :format)
mise :lint            # oxlint + ESLint
mise :test:unit       # Vitest once (if the change is covered)
mise :build           # type-check + Vite production build
```

`mise :test:unit` already runs Vitest once. Watch mode is `mise :test:unit:watch`.

Full gate in one shot: `mise :check` (format:check + lint + type-check + test:unit). Playwright E2E is `mise :test:e2e` and is **not** part of `:check` — start the API yourself first (`e2e/README.md`).

Skip tests only for comment-only or docs-only edits (still run type-check + format:check + lint).

## Rules

- Test public behavior (props, DOM, user actions), not Vue internals.
- Do not change observable behavior unless asked.
- Limit the diff to the files the task needs.

## Checklist

- [ ] `mise :type-check` — zero errors
- [ ] `mise :format:check` — clean
- [ ] `mise :lint` — zero warnings
- [ ] `mise :test:unit` — pass when tests are affected
- [ ] `mise :build` — succeeds
- [ ] Follows @vue-components.mdc and @vue-components-style.mdc
